Site Note: Maakoro-street, Bori Metropolis.

The geophysical survey for this station indicates a six-layer subsurface profile. The resistivity sequence progresses from 168 ohm-m (Layer 1) to 484 ohm-m (Layer 2), dropping to 255 ohm-m (Layer 3), rising to 1109 ohm-m (Layer 4), decreasing to 807 ohm-m (Layer 5), and finally increasing to 8895 ohm-m (Layer 6). Following the specified curve-type notation, the transition sequence (1-2-3, 2-3-4, 3-4-5, and 4-5-6) results in a KHKH pattern. This calculation is consistent with the KHKH-type classification currently recorded in the station files. Drilling teams should note the significant increase in resistivity at the base of the profile.

